  "published": "2026-10-12T17:45:04.75Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.3.0: native binaries move to LiteRT-LM v0.18.0 (Google's official prebuilts), with new runtime packages for linux-arm64 and the x86_64 Android emulator. New: on-device text embeddings (LiteRtEmbeddingEngine, validated with EmbeddingGemma 2) with an IEmbeddingGenerator and Semantic Kernel registration; LiteRtModelInfo reads a model file's metadata without loading it; failed native calls report the runtime's status and reason (LiteRtException.StatusCode); per-conversation speculative decoding, a per-image vision token cap and Metal residency. ActivationDataType now defaults to Float32 (F16 corrupted structured output on the GPUs we measured). Linux no longer needs libvulkan1 for the CPU backend. Behavior changes: EnableYnnpack fails off linux-arm64, a missing cache directory fails engine creation, and a visual token budget above the per-image maximum fails image sends. The managed assembly requires the same-version runtime packages (LiteRT-LM v0.18.0). Full notes: https://github.com/OrihuelaConde/LiteRtLmSharp/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md",
